### Scenario 34 — Multi-claim cascade + claim/penalty list queries, messages, history
### IntelliJ HTTP Client syntax.
### Builds 3 independent claims for the same tenant to exercise PENALTY_APPLIED counters
### and aggregate list endpoints (no auto-deactivation logic in current code — verify by hand).
### Prereq: run 00-smoke.http section 0 first.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@adminEmail = admin@blps.local
@adminPass = adminpass
@landlordEmail = landlord@blps.local
@landlordPass = landpass
@tenantEmail = tenant@blps.local
@tenantPass = tenantpass

### 34.1 Resolve tenant id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Basic {{tenantEmail}} {{tenantPass}}

> {%
client.global.set("tenant34_id", response.body.id);
%}

### 34.2 Claim A — create
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenantId": {{tenant34_id}}, "title": "Cascade A", "description": "First in cascade.", "claimedAmount": 60, "currency": "USD" }

> {%
client.global.set("claimA34_id", response.body.id);
%}

### 34.3 Claim A — drive to PENALTY_APPLIED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA34_id}}/intake-start
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA34_id}}/intake-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestAdditionalInfo": false, "note": "" }

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA34_id}}/assessment
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "penaltyGrounds": true, "assessmentAmount": 50, "assessmentNotes": "A" }

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA34_id}}/tenant-response
Authorization: Basic {{tenantEmail}} {{tenantPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "ack" }

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimA34_id}}/support-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "applyPenalty": true, "penaltyAmount": 50, "penaltyCurrency": "USD", "simulateFailure": false, "resolutionNote": "A" }

